62e-06,-1.1920922133867862e-06],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,785,1346,370,19186,4512,553,279,37906,400,88,25387,61,17,10,19,87,10,21,3,323,400,88,34433,37018,90,16,15170,17,92,87,61,17,37892,10,21,3,31796,518,3501,4930,64,8402,15087,323,4930,66,11991,15087,11,1380,400,66,59,709,264,12947,3555,374,400,66,7409,3,30,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nThe parabolas defined by the equations $y=x^2+4x+6$ and $y=\\frac{1}{2}x^2+x+6$ intersect at points $(a,b)$ and $(c,d)$, where $c\\ge a$. What is $c-a$?","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"506a7281c781d1e23fdbe7d1da6ef6a26c8c406c8d7f8bb4574ea68678f980fc"},"seconds":10.527985334396362,"seed":111410615343399834,"stop":"eos","text":"To find the points of intersection of the parabolas defined by the equations \\(y = x^2 + 4x + 6\\) and \\(y = \\frac{1}{2}x^2 + x + 6\\), we set the equations equal to each other:\n\n\\[x^2 + 4x + 6 = \\frac{1}{2}x^2 + x + 6.\\]\n\nFirst, we eliminate the constant term 6 from both sides:\n\n\\[x^2 + 4x = \\frac{1}{2}x^2 + x.\\]\n\nNext, we eliminate the \\(\\frac{1}{2}x^2\\) term by subtracting \\(\\frac{1}{2}x^2\\) from both sides:\n\n\\[x^2 - \\frac{1}{2}x^2 + 4x - x = 0.\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\\frac{1}{2}x^2 + 3x = 0.\\]\n\nWe can factor out \\(x\\) from the equation:\n\n\\[x\\left(\\frac{1}{2}x + 3\\right) = 0.\\]\n\nThis gives us two solutions:\n\n\\[x = 0 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad \\frac{1}{2}x + 3 = 0.\\]\n\nSolving the second equation for \\(x\\):\n\n\\[\\frac{1}{2}x + 3 = 0 \\implies \\frac{1}{2}x = -3 \\implies x = -6.\\]\n\nSo, the \\(x\\)-coordinates of the points of intersection are \\(x = 0\\) and \\(x = -6\\). Since \\(c \\ge a\\), we have \\(c = 0\\) and \\(a = -6\\). Therefore, the difference \\(c - a\\) is:\n\n\\[c - a = 0 - (-6) = 6.\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\\boxed{6}.\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{6}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"algebra:930"}
